cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Quaternion-Monoid Algebra: A Compositional Algebra over
  Fixed-Width Quaternionic-Symbolic State Packets
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the
  metadata from this file.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Cody
    family-names: Churchwell
    alias: consigcody94
repository-code: 'https://github.com/consigcody94/quaternion-monoid-algebra'
abstract: >-
  A compositional algebra over a fixed-width packet structure carrying a
  unit quaternion, symbolic metadata fields, and a positive scaling factor.
  Defines a closed associative binary operation with two-sided identity,
  making the packet space a monoid, with an additional empirically-observed
  topology-preservation property under iterated composition. Includes CPU
  and GPU reference implementations with bit-exact correspondence, a
  vectorized batch API with tree reduction, a library of verified
  alternative sub-field constructions, formal topology notes with
  machine-checked proofs, and a layered validation suite (property-based
  tests via Hypothesis, an eight-test property runner, and seven stress
  tests including real TUM RGB-D and EuRoC MAV data), and three application
  examples (agent state evolution, multi-source state composition,
  algebraic chain verification).
keywords:
  - quaternion
  - monoid
  - compositional algebra
  - topological data analysis
  - state evolution
  - audit chain
license: MIT
